stration"],"visibility":"public","forks":18214,"open_issues":1927,"watchers":47308,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/pulls/70081","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/70081","diff_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/70081.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/70081.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"<!-- SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\r\n     https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0 -->\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nThe Task Execution API's `set_xcom` endpoint implicitly has access to the current task instance identifiers through the injected JWT token. Removing the task identifiers (`dag_id`, `run_id`, `task_id`) from the URL simplifies routing, prevents clients from providing conflicting or invalid identifiers, and enforces zero-trust security where a task instance can only write its own XComs.\r\n\r\nThis refactor:\r\n- Updates the `has_xcom_access` dependency to handle write requests gracefully without requiring `dag_id` in the URL path.\r\n- Modifies the `set_xcom` endpoint to query identifiers securely from the database via the token.\r\n- Cleans up `client.xcoms.set` in the Task SDK to use the simplified URL format.\r\n\r\ncloses: #70080\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n##### Was generative AI tooling used to co-author this PR?\r\n\r\n- [x] Yes (please specify the tool below)\r\n\r\nGenerated-by: [Gemini] following [the guidelines](https://github.com/apache/airflow/blob/main/contributing-docs/05_pull_requests.rst#gen-ai-assisted-contributions)\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/70081/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/70081/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/comments/5127203525","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow/issues/70080#issuecomment-5127203525","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/70080","id":5127203525,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAgUK288AAAABMZrqxQ","user":{"login":"shivaam","id":6463385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0NjMzODU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6463385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shivaam","html_url":"https://github.com/shivaam","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shivaam/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shivaam/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shivaam/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shivaam/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shivaam/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shivaam/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shivaam/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shivaam/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shivaam/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-30T06:02:21Z","updated_at":"2026-07-30T06:04:19Z","body":"I have started working on a compatible first slice for this issue. The plan is to keep the existing POST route for older Task SDK clients, validate its Dag/run/task/map identity against the TaskInstance identified by the JWT, and use the token-resolved identity for the write. I will keep the read-route source identifiers unchanged because cross-task, cross-Dag, historical, and mapped XCom pulls rely on them.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/comments/5127203525/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimi